      "title": "TXN Q3 Earnings Beat Estimates on Strong Analog, Data Center Demand",
      "summary": "Texas Instruments (TXN) reported Q3 2026 earnings of $2.62 per share, up 77% year-over-year and beating estimates by 9.2%. Revenues surged 28% to $6.06B, driven by strong growth in analog (32%), data center (95%), and industrial (40%+) segments. Operating margins expanded to 47.5%, and the company raised its dividend by 7% for the 23rd consecutive year. Q4 guidance ranges from $5.80B to $6.30B in revenues.",
